Origin: from 3543;
Meaning: feeble, obscure
KJV renders: somewhat dark, darkish, wax dim, heaviness, smoking.

H3545.strongs:
Origin: feminine of 3544;
Meaning: properly, a weakening; figuratively, alleviation, i.e. cure
KJV renders: healing.

H3546.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) a root corresponding to and 3557;
Meaning: to be able
KJV renders: be able, could.

H3547.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root, apparently meaning to mediate in religious services; but used only as denominative from 3548;
Meaning: to officiate as a priest; figuratively, to put on regalia
KJV renders: deck, be (do the office of a, execute the, minister in the) priest('s office).

H3548.strongs:
Origin: active participle of 3547;
Meaning: literally one officiating, a priest; also (by courtesy) an acting priest (although a layman)
KJV renders: chief ruler, × own, priest, prince, principal officer.

H3550.strongs:
Origin: from 3547;
Meaning: priesthood
KJV renders: priesthood, priest's office.

H3551.strongs:
Origin: (Aramaic) from a root corresponding to 3854 in the sense of piercing;
Meaning: a window (as a perforation)
KJV renders: window.

H3552.strongs:
Origin: of foreign derivation;
Meaning: Kub, a country near Egypt
KJV renders: Chub.

H3553.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root meaning to be high or rounded;
Meaning: a helmet (as arched)
KJV renders: helmet. Compare 6959.

H3554.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: properly, to prick or penetrate; hence, to blister (as smarting or eating into)
KJV renders: burn.

H3555.strongs:
Origin: from 3554;
Meaning: a branding
KJV renders: burning.

H3556.strongs:
Origin: probably from the same as 3522 (in the sense of rolling) or 3554 (in the sense of blazing);
Meaning: a star (as round or as shining); figuratively, a prince
KJV renders: star(-gazer).

H3557.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: properly, to keep in; hence, to measure; figuratively, to maintain (in various senses)
KJV renders: (be able to, can) abide, bear, comprehend, contain, feed, forbearing, guide, hold(-ing in), nourish(-er), be present, make provision, receive, sustain, provide sustenance (victuals).

H3558.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root meaning to store away;
Meaning: a jewel (probably gold beads)
KJV renders: tablet.

H3559.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: properly, to be erect (i.e. stand perpendicular); hence (causatively) to set up, in a great variety of applications, whether literal (establish, fix, prepare, apply), or figurative (appoint, render sure, proper or prosperous)
KJV renders: certain(-ty), confirm, direct, faithfulness, fashion, fasten, firm, be fitted, be fixed, frame, be meet, ordain, order, perfect, (make) preparation, prepare (self), provide, make provision, (be, make) ready, right, set (aright, fast, forth), be stable, (e-) stablish, stand, tarry, × very deed.

H3560.strongs:
Origin: probably from 3559; established;
Meaning: Kun, a place in Syria
KJV renders: Chun.

H3561.strongs:
Origin: from 3559;
Meaning: something prepared, i.e. a sacrificial wafer
KJV renders: cake.

H3562.strongs:
Origin: from 3559 and 3050; Jah has sustained;
Meaning: Conanjah, the name of two Israelites
KJV renders: Conaniah, Cononiah. Compare 3663.

H3563.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root meaning to hold together;
Meaning: a cup (as a container), often figuratively, a lot (as if a potion); also some unclean bird, probably an owl (perhaps from the cup-like cavity of its eye)
KJV renders: cup, (small) owl. Compare 3599.

H3564.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root meaning properly, to dig through;
Meaning: a pot or furnace (as if excavated)
KJV renders: furnace. Compare 3600.

H3565.strongs:
Origin: from 3564 and 6227; furnace of smoke;
Meaning: Cor-Ashan, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Chorashan.

H3566.strongs:
Origin: or (Ezra 1:1 (last time),2) כֹּרֶשׁ; from the Persian;
Meaning: Koresh (or Cyrus), the Persian king
KJV renders: Cyrus.

H3568.strongs:
Origin: probably of foreign origin;
Meaning: Cush (or Ethiopia), the name of a son of Ham, and of his territory; also of an Israelite
KJV renders: Chush, Cush, Ethiopia.

H3569.strongs:
Origin: patronymically from 3568;
Meaning: a Cushite, or descendant of Cush
KJV renders: Cushi, Cushite, Ethiopian(-s).

H3570.strongs:
Origin: the same as 3569;
Meaning: Cushi, the name of two Israelites
KJV renders: Cushi.

H3571.strongs:
Origin: feminine of 3569;
Meaning: a Cushite woman
KJV renders: Ethiopian.

H3572.strongs:
Origin: perhaps from 3568;
Meaning: Cushan, a region of Arabia
KJV renders: Cushan.

H3573.strongs:
Origin: apparently from 3572 and the dual of 7564; Cushan of double wickedness;
Meaning: Cushan-Rishathajim, a Mesopotamian king
KJV renders: Chushan-rishathayim.

H3574.strongs:
Origin: from 3787;
Meaning: prosperity; in plural freedom
KJV renders: × chain.

H3575.strongs:
Origin: or (feminine) כּוּתָה; of foreign origin;
Meaning: Cuth or Cuthah, a province of Assyria
KJV renders: Cuth.

H3576.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to lie (i.e. deceive), literally or figuratively
KJV renders: fail, (be found a, make a) liar, lie, lying, be in vain.

H3577.strongs:
Origin: from 3576;
Meaning: falsehood; literally (untruth) or figuratively (idol)
KJV renders: deceitful, false, leasing, liar, lie, lying.

H3578.strongs:
Origin: from 3576; fallacious;
Meaning: Cozeba, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Choseba.

H3579.strongs:
Origin: from 3576; false;
Meaning: Cozbi, a Midianitess
KJV renders: Cozbi.

H3580.strongs:
Origin: from 3576; falsified;
Meaning: Kezib, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Chezib.

H3581.strongs:
Origin: or (Daniel 11:6) כּוֹחַ; from an unused root meaning to be firm;
Meaning: vigor, literally (force, in a good or a bad sense) or figuratively (capacity, means, produce); also (from its hardiness) a large lizard
KJV renders: ability, able, chameleon, force, fruits, might, power(-ful), strength, substance, wealth.

H3582.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to secrete, by act or word; hence (intensively) to destroy
KJV renders: conceal, cut down (off), desolate, hide.

H3583.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to paint (with stibium)
KJV renders: paint.

H3584.strongs:
Origin: a primitive root;
Meaning: to be untrue, in word (to lie, feign, disown) or deed (to disappoint, fail, cringe)
KJV renders: deceive, deny, dissemble, fail, deal falsely, be found liars, (be-) lie, lying, submit selves.

H3585.strongs:
Origin: from 3584;
Meaning: literally a failure of flesh, i.e. emaciation; figuratively, hypocrisy
KJV renders: leanness, lies, lying.

H3586.strongs:
Origin: from 3584;
Meaning: faithless
KJV renders: lying.

H3587.strongs:
Origin: from 3554;
Meaning: a brand or scar
KJV renders: burning.

H3588.strongs:
Origin: a primitive particle (the full form of the prepositional prefix) indicating causal relations of all kinds, antecedent or consequent;
Meaning: (by implication) very widely used as a relative conjunction or adverb (as below); often largely modified by other particles annexed
KJV renders: and, (forasmuch, inasmuch, where-) as, assured(-ly), but, certainly, doubtless, else, even, except, for, how, (because, in, so, than) that, nevertheless, now, rightly, seeing, since, surely, then, therefore, (al-) though, till, truly, until, when, whether, while, whom, yea, yet.

H3589.strongs:
Origin: from a primitive root meaning to strike;
Meaning: a crushing; figuratively, calamity
KJV renders: destruction.

H3590.strongs:
Origin: from the same as 3589 (compare 3539);
Meaning: properly, something struck off, i.e. a spark (as struck)
KJV renders: spark.

H3592.strongs:
Origin: the same as 3591;
Meaning: Kidon, a place in Palestine
KJV renders: Chidon.

H3593.strongs:
Origin: of uncertain derivation;
Meaning: perhaps tumult
KJV renders: battle.

H3594.strongs:
Origin: from 3559;
Meaning: properly, a statue, i.e. idol; but used (by euphemism) for some heathen deity (perhaps corresponding to Priapus or Baal-peor)
KJV renders: Chiun.

H3595.strongs:
Origin: or כִּיֹּר; from the same as 3564;
Meaning: properly, something round (as excavated or bored), i.e. a chafing-dish for coals or a caldron for cooking; hence (from similarity of form) a washbowl; also (for the same reason) a pulpit or platform
KJV renders: hearth, laver, pan, scaffold.

H3596.strongs:
Origin: or כֵּלַי; from 3557 in the sense of withholding;
Meaning: niggardly
KJV renders: churl.

H3597.strongs:
Origin: from an unused root meaning to clap or strike with noise;
Meaning: a club or sledge-hammer
KJV renders: hammer.

H3598.strongs:
Origin: from the same as 3558;
Meaning: a cluster of stars, i.e. the Pleiades
KJV renders: Pleiades, seven stars.

H3599.strongs:
Origin: a form for 3563;
Meaning: a cup; also a bag for money or weights
KJV renders: bag, cup, purse.

bdb:
כִּיס n.m. Pr 1:14 bag, purse (perh. kindred with כּוֹס, q.v.; Ar. Arabic (prob. fr. Pers. Persian Lane 2640); Eth. Ethiopic NH כִּיס; Aram. כִּיסָא, Syriac; Palm. מן כיסה from his purse = at his own expense, Vog p. 13 al.)—bag, in which were carried:
weights (v. אֶבֶן 5) Dt 25:13 Mi 6:11 Pr 16:11;
money, i.e. a purse Is 46:6 Pr 1:14.
